From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:52:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 40/41] Inkling-2 support and optimisation (rdna3 ink-r366, 58
 commits squashed)

Inkling-2-Mini (arch inkling2 / inkling2_loop) on our stack: upstream support plus our engine work,
squashed from rdna3 branch ink-r366 (tip 530307838d) over production cand-r366 7e8e853c91.
FINDINGS 1113-1117, 1151-1179 (rocm ~/FINDINGS.md) hold the per-change measurements.

Upstream (ggml-org) and Unsloth pieces, as squashed diffs:
- ggml-org #32694 (Inkling 2 Mini), #32669, #32763, #32704, #32799, #32855, #32940, #32897;
  #32833 applied then reverted (net zero); #32751 (inkling2 tensor split, open); #32218 (DSpark
  drafter, merged 33aeb17f8); #33073 (DFlash2).
- Unsloth #385, #395, #396, and fusions #401 #402 #411 #412 #414.

Ours, bit-exact unless noted, each with a kill switch:
- Inkling graph: LLAMA_INKLING_GRAPH_LEAN, LLAMA_INKLING_LEVEL_ORDER, LLAMA_INKLING_LMHEAD_SPLIT,
  LLAMA_INKLING_POS_BIAS, LLAMA_INKLING_DECODE_POS_BIAS; LLAMA_INKLING_MIX_T (output-changing, KLD-checked);
  LLAMA_INKLING_TABLE_2D (opt-in).
- CUDA fusions: clip-scaled (+pair), ctl gate, multi-GEMV, ycat GEMV, rel-mask, rel-table
  (GGML_CUDA_REL_TABLE_FUSION), depth-mix (+RMS; GGML_CUDA_DEPTH_MIX_ODD is output-changing, KLD 0.0015),
  conv chain (+pair, residual epilogue, state gather), K/V store, sibling GEMV, RMS_NORM+Q8_1 siblings,
  F32 small-K GEMV (GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_* / GGML_CUDA_* switches as listed in the code).
- Flash attention: derived-mask per-query-tile bitmap (GGML_CUDA_FA_DERIVED_TILED), GQA-3 fold for decode
  and verify widths (GGML_CUDA_FA_TILE_GQA3).
- Shared kernels touched (all models): MMB NVFP4 register-table dequant + prefetch (GGML_CUDA_MMB_FP4_PERM;
  = Stew PR #379); MoE GEMV rows-per-block packing on RDNA3_0 (GGML_CUDA_MOE_RPB_PACK); RDNA3 grid-size
  stall pad band (GGML_CUDA_GRID_STALL_PAD); Q8_0 two rows on RDNA3_0 (GGML_MMVQ_RDNA3_TWO_ROWS); verify-band
  norm+Q8_1 fusion on RDNA3_0 (GGML_CUDA_FUSE_Q8_1_VERIFY).  The RDNA3-only gates do not run on RDNA4.
- LLAMA_KV_BASE_TYPE=<type>: K/V type of the iSWA non-SWA cache only (opt-in, output-changing; q8_0 KLD
  0.0013 on Inkling); the pos-bias FA path accepts Q8_0 K/V.

7900 XTX (gfx1100), Inkling-2-Mini UD-IQ4_XS, 1 GPU: pp512 ~2500, tg64 83.4 / 73.1 / 67.0 t/s at
0 / 32K / 64K (mainline 1280 / 53.6); DSpark decode on a 28K prompt 81.1 t/s; two concurrent 34K+39K
prompts 44.3 s.  Greedy refs (inks.sh, UD-IQ4_XS): long 1863dd6f1f8b, short 7bda2aa2cc87; KLD vs
current mainline 0.0021 (ub 512) / 0.0024 (ub 1).
2x R9700 (gfx1201), UD-Q8_K_XL, -sm tensor, -ub 2048: pp 2253 / tg 69.7 t/s at 0K, 981 / 56.1 at 128K;
with DSpark n_max 2, tg 116 at 0K. Flash-Next production outputs unchanged (ours/README.md, Validation).
